This is an Nx monorepo managed with pnpm (Node 22+).
`apps/web` is the Next.js 16 App Router dashboard (also hosts the MCP server).
`apps/trigger` contains Trigger.dev v4 tasks and agents.
`apps/*-worker` and `apps/cloudflare-agent` are Cloudflare Workers.
`packages/platform` is the shared domain layer; `packages/ui` is the design system.
`supabase/` contains migrations and config for Supabase.
Use pnpm for package management. Never use npm or yarn.

## Code Style and Structure

Write concise, technical TypeScript code with accurate examples.
Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes.
Prefer iteration and modularisation over code duplication.
Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError).
Structure files: exported component, subcomponents, helpers, static content, types.
Put shared domain logic in `packages/platform`, not in individual apps.

## Naming Conventions

Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., components/auth-wizard).
Favour named exports for components.
Reuse components from `@stuntdouble/ui` before creating new ones.

## TypeScript Usage

Use TypeScript for all code.
Avoid enums; use maps or union types instead.
Validate external input with Zod.
Always check types and fix type errors before completion.

## Syntax and Formatting

Use the "function" keyword for pure functions.
Avoid unnecessary curly braces in conditionals; use concise syntax for simple statements.
Use declarative JSX.
Run ESLint and Prettier before committing.

## UI and Styling

Use `@stuntdouble/ui` (shadcn/ui on Radix UI) and Tailwind CSS v4.
Use Continuity icons from `@stunt-double/icons`.
Implement responsive design with a mobile-first approach.
Support light and dark themes via theme tokens, not hard-coded colours.
Use Next.js layout.tsx to share common structure across routes.

## Performance Optimisation

Minimise 'use client', 'useEffect', and 'setState'; favour React Server Components (RSC).
Wrap client components in Suspense with a fallback.
Use dynamic loading for non-critical components.
Optimise images: use WebP, include size data, implement lazy loading.

## Database Querying & Data Model Creation

Use the Supabase clients exported from `@stuntdouble/platform`.
Use @supabase/ssr and @supabase/supabase-js; never use "@supabase/auth-helpers-nextjs".
Create migrations in `./supabase/migrations/` with a timestamp prefix generated from the current time.
`database.ts` is generated; never edit it by hand. Regenerate types via the Supabase CLI or MCP.
Enable RLS on every new table.

## AI and Agents

Use the Vercel AI SDK for model calls; use the Claude Agent SDK for agentic runs.
Run long or browser-driven work as Trigger.dev tasks, not in request handlers.
Gate MCP tools by OAuth scope.

## Key Conventions

Optimise Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, INP).
Follow the Next.js App Router conventions for data fetching, rendering and routing.
Use Vercel Flags for feature flags.
Use Pino for structured logging.

## Evaluation

Ensure all imported components are valid exports of the package.
Add any new dependencies with pnpm to the correct workspace package.
Check and correct all errors before finishing.
